 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Totally normal. You don't need order anything fancy. Order what you enjoy, and it's slow, keep it light and friendly. The really good restaurants expect lots of food coming your way. They' trained to handle it. Take small bites and focus on the flavors, that's what they care about. Classic for the first time meal. Black or white shirt, nice jeans. Most people don't. The menu will tell you which courses to start with. And if you' unsure, ask to skip a dish and use the ingredients as garnish. Not necessary. The cooked food is what matters. The tasting menu gives you more, so it' worth considering though.",
